{
  "description": "The shared secret-name rule marks these members because their names contain `password`, `secret`, `token`, `credential` or `encryption key`, but each one is not a secret: it holds the name of a Secret Manager secret or version, a Cloud KMS key, a Credential resource, or a Cloud Storage URI of an encrypted file, so the secret itself is never in the field. This removes the mark.",
  "patches": [
    {
